# Trivy ignore file — accepted findings, each with justification.

# AVD-DS-0002: "Specify a USER instruction (non-root)".
# The entrypoint must start as root so nginx can bind 80/443 and certbot can write
# /etc/letsencrypt. It immediately drops the backend — the main attack surface
# (auth, HTTP proxy, RBI) — to the unprivileged 'endoriumfort' user via gosu, and
# nginx runs its workers non-root. Full non-root would require moving nginx to
# high ports and reworking deployments; tracked separately.
AVD-DS-0002
